# Pull Request Rules

When creating pull requests, always follow these rules:

## Title
- Use conventional commit format: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, etc.
- Keep the title short and descriptive of the change.
- **Do not** include Linear ticket numbers (e.g. `LIT-706`, `[PINT-123]`) in the title. Reference the ticket only in the PR description body.

## Description
- Be concise and to the point.
- Use bullet points over long paragraphs.

## Required Label
- Every PR **must** include the label `Team: Live Interaction`.
- Add it at creation time: `gh pr create --label "Team: Live Interaction"`.
- **Do not** create a PR without this label. If it cannot be applied, ask the user for guidance before proceeding.

## Draft
- Always create PRs as drafts: `gh pr create --draft`.
